# Jumps to pRef depending on its type; only $modify() of a method is fully reliable.

If isclear(pRef)
	OK message {No target to show.}
	Quit method
End If
# type via $group (single step, explicit). NB a GROUP itself has $group.$name='' ,
# so check the ref's OWN name to spot a $methods / $objs group as target.
Set reference ref to pRef.$group
Calculate grpName as ref.$name
Switch grpName
	Case '$methods'
		Do pRef.$modify(1) ## a method -> straight to it (reliable)
	Case '$objs'
		If pRef.$methods.$count>0
			Do pRef.$methods.$first().$modify(1) ## object's own method (F3 for layout)
		Else
			Do iTools.$modify(pRef,kFalse) ## object without method -> layout editor
		End If
	Default
		If pRef.$name='$methods' ## the methods GROUP itself -> method editor
			Do iTools.$modify(pRef,kTrue)
		Else
			Do iTools.$modify(pRef,kFalse) ## class / objs group / vardef -> layout editor
		End If
End Switch
Quit method